{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"c652c6bf27bb6c4677f7e80a26cb56d9e39f51ce95abbda82376baa02ed0ef48","digest":{"component_or_area":"autodeploy secrets-refresh path (reviewbot durable-tickets)","key_entities":["infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh","infra/terraform/ssm.tf","SECRETS_PATHS","BOT_PATHS","REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT","/rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat","infra/compose/.env","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py","secrets-fetch-failed","record_backoff_failure"],"problem_keywords":["env delivery gap","secrets fetch on deploy","ssm-backed env keys","autodeploy","fail-safe deploy abort","review-bot redeploy","code_review artifact emission"],"propositions":["autodeploy.sh rsync-excludes infra/compose/.env and never re-runs fetch-secrets.sh, so newly-added SSM-backed env keys never reach the box on deploy without a manual boot.","autodeploy must re-run fetch-secrets.sh before 'docker compose up' when BOT_PATHS or a new SECRETS_PATHS trigger (fetch-secrets.sh, ssm.tf) changes, so secrets-only changes recreate the container with the new .env.","On any fetch-secrets/SSM failure the deploy must abort fail-safe: emit err marker, record_backoff_failure, leave .env intact and the running bot untouched with no rollback needed.","code_review artifacts are emitted and pushed from prod reviews without emission-failed warnings.","The SSM PAT slot holds a broad classic repo-scope token rather than the specified fine-grained contents:write-only token; least-privilege swap is recommended but human-mintable only.","A fresh entrypoint clone of the tickets branch is write-dead (gitignored id, missing git identity) causing silent commit failure, tracked separately as bug d220."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785205019068478416,"uuid":"2fc0f1a2-da23-40dd-9fe5-e69a39207de5"}